pages.content:
RefineUI is the unified design system for Pelagornis products. Foundation variables become `@refineui/tokens`. UI is `@refineui/react`. The Web Kit you design against is the React you ship.

## Architecture

- **[Foundations](/foundations/)** — Visual language, design tokens, and layout
- **[Components](/components/)** — Actions, Forms, Navigation, Feedback, Overlays, Data Display, Content, Layout
- **[Development](/development/)** — Installation, theming, and motion in product code
- **[AI & Tools](/ai-tools/)** — DESIGN.md, llms.txt, Skill, Doctor, MCP

## Install

<PackageInstallFull />

## Stylesheet

Load token CSS and component interaction styles once at the app root:

```css
@import "@refineui/tokens/tailwind.css";
@import "@refineui/web-icons/dist/fonts/refineui-system-icons.css";
@import "@refineui/react/refineui.css";
```

Or in JS:

```tsx
```

## Example

```tsx
export function Example() {
  return (
    <Card>
      <Input placeholder="Email" />
      <Button variant="primary">Continue</Button>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

## Next

- [Foundations](/foundations/) — tokens and layout
- [Components](/components/) — interactive UI primitives
- [Development / Installation](/development/installation/) — deeper setup notes
- [Iconography](https://github.com/pelagornis/refineui-system-icons) — system icons (separate site / repo)

